(a) The initial value is:
$\begin{aligned}Q(0)&=30+10e^0\\&=40.\end{aligned}$
Here $A>0$ and $k>0$. The curve starts above $Q=30$, increases and becomes progressively steeper. It grows without bound, so there is no finite limiting value.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\begin{axis}[width=70mm,height=52mm,axis lines=left,xlabel={$t$},ylabel={$Q$},xmin=0,xmax=9,ymin=0,ymax=90,xtick=\empty,ytick={30,40},tick label style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},clip=false]
